{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:74438",
  "title": "Moderate: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-03 12:04:21"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-07 00:15:21"
  },
  "severity": "Moderate",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: RDMA/uverbs: Validate wqe_size before using it in ib_uverbs_post_send (CVE-2026-45856)\n\n* kernel: KVM: SVM: Fix page overflow in sev_dbg_crypt() for ENCRYPT path (CVE-2026-63794)\n\n* kernel: futex: Fix race on the initial mm-\u003efutex.phash.ref allocation (CVE-2026-80775)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Backport of protocol attribute to IP addresses (IFA_PROTO) [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-169936)\n\n* try_charge_memcg() refactor in kernel 5.14.0-687.36.1 causes premature memcg OOM with GiB of clean page cache present [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-269060)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
